{:adr-id "2610000000"
 :title "cloud-itonami-isic-1430 (manufacture of knitted and crocheted apparel) plant-operations-coordination actor"
 :status :accepted
 :date "2026-07-16"
 :deciders ["Jun Kawasaki (agent-executed, standing authorization)"]
 :related ["ADR-2607121000" "ADR-2607011000"]

 :context
 "ISIC 1430 ('Manufacture of knitted and crocheted apparel') had no existing
  implementation -- gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-1430 returned 404
  before this task began. Live kotoba-lang/industry registry re-verified fresh
  before work began: :name 'Manufacture of knitted and crocheted apparel' confirmed
  for {:id \"1430\"}, distinct from sibling 1410 ('Manufacture of wearing apparel,
  except fur apparel', cut-and-sew, already :implemented). 1430 covers garments
  knitted/crocheted directly to shape (circular/flat-knitting machine lines
  producing shaped garment panels, then linked together), distinct from 1410's
  cut-and-sew process. The registry's pre-existing 1430 entry carried stale
  placeholder metadata: :maturity :spec, :repo gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-C1430,
  :business-id cloud-itonami-C1430 (wrong org and wrong naming convention) --
  corrected in place as part of this task's registry edit. Built from
  cloud-itonami-isic-1410 (apparel.*, wearing apparel except fur) as the
  module-structure template, adapted from cut-and-sew to knitwear manufacturing.
  Note: 1410's own README/blueprint.edn still read :blueprint/'no actor
  implementation yet' despite the repo's actual passing implementation and the
  registry's :maturity :implemented for 1410 -- a pre-existing documentation
  staleness bug in the reference repo, not reproduced here."

 :scope-exclusions
 ["operating circular- or flat-knitting machines (licensed knitting engineer/technician exclusive authority)"
  "setting knitting parameters (gauge, tension, stitch length, RPM, etc.)"
  "design decisions about patterns, yarns, or garment shaping"
  "yarn/fabric quality approval (mill's responsibility)"]

 :decision
 "Implement cloud-itonami-isic-1430 with Governor, Facts, Registry, Store, Advisor,
  Phase, Sim (mirrors cloud-itonami-isic-1410 module-for-module, adapted from
  cut-and-sew apparel to knitwear manufacturing -- knitwear.* namespace,
  circular/flat-knitting-line vocabulary):
  - Governor (knitwear-governor): HARD invariants (op-not-allowed via closed
    4-op allowlist, effect-not-propose, plant-not-verified/batch-not-verified
    for both direct batch-logging and shipment-coordination resolved through the
    shipment record, process-control-forbidden as a permanent block on
    knitting-line-equipment-control language) + ESCALATE invariants
    (safety-concern-escalates always for flag-safety-concern, escalate for low
    confidence < 0.6 or high-stakes shipment actuation)
  - Facts: per-jurisdiction compliance catalog (Vietnam/Bangladesh/USA) with real
    official spec-basis citations including ISO 11111-1:2016 textile-machinery
    safety -- honest, non-exhaustive coverage
  - Registry: proposal-drafting helpers + independent hard-invariant/protected-op
    predicates sharing the same closed allowlist as the governor
  - Store: in-memory MemStore (plants, production batches, shipments,
    maintenance-log) plus a shipment-batch-verified? helper that correctly
    resolves shipment -> batch -> plant (fixing a latent gap observed in 1410's
    reference governor, which looked up the shipment ID directly in the batch
    table instead of resolving through the shipment record)
  - Advisor: mock advisor drafting all four ops, :effect :propose only
  - Phase: langgraph-clj-style phase table (advisor -> governor -> decision ->
    hold/complete)
  - Sim: demo runner with a working -main
  - Operations: log-production-batch (knitting/linking batch, output-quality data
    logging), schedule-maintenance (knitting-line-equipment maintenance
    scheduling), flag-safety-concern (equipment-safety/quality-defect concern,
    ALWAYS escalates), coordinate-shipment (outbound shipment coordination,
    high-stakes actuation)
  - Tests: 31 tests / 107 assertions, all green
  - All .cljc (portable, no JVM-only interop -- clojure.string/lower-case used
    instead of .toLowerCase), AGPL-3.0-or-later
  - GitHub repo created directly as cloud-itonami-isic-1430 (confirmed 404 before
    creation, no rename/fallback needed)
  - Registry 1430 entry: :maturity :spec -> :implemented, :repo/:business-id
    corrected from the gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-C1430 placeholder to
    cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-1430, ADR reference added"

 :consequences
 {:positive
  ["Knitted/crocheted apparel manufacturing (1430) plant-operations-coordination
    now genuinely implemented and fully tested, distinct from and non-duplicative
    of sibling 1410's cut-and-sew scope"
   "Scope boundary (plant operations/logistics/compliance paperwork only, never
    knitting-line equipment operation) hardcoded in governor's
    process-control-forbidden check, not just asserted in prose"
   "Safety-concern escalation and high-stakes shipment escalation are core design
    invariants, structurally separate from the hard non-overridable invariants"
   "Portable .cljc, zero JVM-only constructs, clj-kondo 0 errors"
   "Registry's stale placeholder repo/business-id metadata corrected to the
    fleet-standard naming as part of the same maturity-flip change"]
  :negative
  ["Real persistent store (Datomic/kotoba-server) is a follow-up (in-memory for now)"
   "langgraph-clj StateGraph wiring is phase-table scaffolding, matching 1410's own
    stub status; production integration pending"]}

